{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Behold, tomorrow I am bringing the locusts.</b> The commentators said that there were many days between the plague of hail and the plague of locusts, for the sake of <b>that which grows for you from the field</b> (Exodus 10:5). In my opinion there were not many days between them, but only a few, for it is well known that the judgment of the Egyptians did not last more than a year, as will be known from the years of Moses our teacher, as we learned in tractate Eduyyot (2:10): the judgment of the Egyptians in Egypt was twelve months. And so He said (Exodus 10:5), <b>the remnant of what was left to you from the hail</b>, and it is written (Exodus 10:12), \"what the hail left\" — for that year itself was [the time of the hail]; if so, the hail was in the month of Adar in that year, no earlier, for the barley was in the stage of aviv (early growth) and the wheat was in the stage of afilah (late growth), and it would not harm it if the hail struck what had sprouted from it, for it would grow back and sprout anew. And the vine had not yet blossomed and the trees had not yet budded, and therefore Scripture said (Exodus 9:25), \"and it shattered every tree of the field,\" for it broke the branches and the foliage. And afterwards, in the month of Nisan, the wheat and the spelt grew, and that is the remnant left to them from the hail, and the trees began to put forth blossom and the buds appeared. And this is the meaning of \"that which grows,\" for the locusts came and ate their blossoms and destroyed everything, so that they left them no blossom or bud, and in this very month they were redeemed. And Scripture's statement (Exodus 10:15), \"and all the fruit of the tree,\" refers to the bud that would have become fruit, as it says (ibid.), \"all the verdure of the tree.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:24.349027181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}